<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's Indian Pacific to resume Friday.</title>
<headline>Australia's Indian Pacific to resume Friday.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's transcontinental rail service, the Indian Pacific, was due to resume services as scheduled on Friday following an end to industrial action, the Australian National (AN) railway said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The strike by Public Transport Union members in Western Australia, which began on Monday, saw the cancellation of an eastbound service from Perth to Sydney and the disruption of the westbound service.</p>
<p>AN said in a statement the strike had not been specifically targeted at the rail service.</p>
<p>It was part of a union campaign against new Western Australian industrial relations laws. -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
